# The production model. Everything the two deployments analyse and every
# trading decision they make runs on this build.
#
# It was missing from this directory until 2026-08-26 — built once by hand and
# never written down, so the one model that mattered was the one that could not
# be rebuilt from source control. The four experimental Modelfiles beside it
# were all committed.
#
# 96k of context, which stock gemma4:e2b does not have. At the default context
# the tool-call history was truncated out from under the reasoning loop and a
# ZBH analysis never terminated (GraphRecursionError). At 96k that does not
# happen. No num_batch override is needed: gemma4's sliding-window attention
# keeps the compute graph small, so this loads 36/36 layers on an 8 GiB card
# using 1.9 GiB. Do not reason from that to a Llama of the same size — those
# need PARAMETER num_batch 64 or they spill to the CPU.
FROM gemma4:e2b
PARAMETER num_ctx 98304

# Sampling is Gemma's own recommendation, unchanged: temperature 1 / top_k 64
# / top_p 0.95. Google publishes those as the standard configuration for all
# use cases (https://ollama.com/library/gemma4), so they are not left alone out
# of caution — they are the documented setting.
#
# **This file briefly carried temperature 0.15 / top_k 20 / top_p 0.9 on
# 2026-08-26, and that was a mistake worth recording.** The reasoning was that
# the agent researched on only about half of identical passes and low
# temperature made it consistent. The inference was wrong. Running the same
# prompt against gemma4:e4b at Gemma's stock sampling gave a research decision
# 4 times out of 4 — so the inconsistency was the 2B model's capability, not
# the temperature, and turning the temperature down treated the symptom while
# moving production off the documented configuration mid-experiment.
#
# **Keep this finding, which is independent and still true.** The app reaches
# Ollama through the OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint, and that
# endpoint silently ignores `temperature` in the request body. Measured
# 2026-08-26 on one pinned card: via /v1 the same prompt answered differently
# 2-3 times in 5 whatever temperature was asked for, while the native
# /api/chat with options.temperature=0 was identical 4 times out of 4.
# TRADINGAGENTS_TEMPERATURE therefore does nothing. If sampling ever does need
# to change, this file is the only channel that reaches the model.
